  "tripSharingLabel": "Share my trips",
  "tripSharingSubtitle": "Helps fix bus routes and missing footpaths.",
  "tripSharingInfoTooltip": "What this shares",
  "tripSharingInfoTitle": "What \"Share my trips\" does",
  "tripSharingInfoBody": "Only while you follow a trip in Guidy, it records:\n\n• The route you rode: the lines and stops, when you reached each step, and your phone's GPS along the way. This is how Guidy learns that a bus or microbus now takes a different street, and fixes the line for everyone.\n\n• The paths you walk on the trip's walking steps. Before anything is sent, the first and last 50 metres of each walk are cut off, so your home, work and other doors stay out of it. This finds footpaths and crossings missing from the map.\n\nNothing is recorded when you're not following a trip. What's sent is kept with the trip it came from, without your name, and deleted after 180 days. Deleting your account removes what ties it to you.\n\nThis is on by default, as our Terms and Privacy Policy say. You can turn it off here at any time: nothing more is recorded, and anything not sent yet is deleted.",
  "tripSharingInfoOk": "OK",
  "tripShareAskTitle": "Help improve Guidy",
  "tripShareAskBody": "Share this trip's path to help fix bus routes and missing footpaths?",
  "tripShareAskYes": "Share",
  "tripShareAskNo": "Not now",
  "whatsNewTitle": "What's new in Guidy",
  "whatsNewOk": "Got it",
  "commuteInfoTooltip": "About commute notifications",
  "commuteInfoTitle": "Commute notifications",
  "commuteInfoBody": "Guidy watches the trip between your saved Home and Work, both ways. Save Home and Work, then plan that trip once: Guidy remembers its lines and looks them up again every two weeks.\n\nIt can send two kinds of alert, each with its own switch:\n• Easier times to travel: when one of your lines runs much more often than usual (mornings 5-11, afternoons 1-9). If your lines have no timetable, it warns you before the morning (7:00) and evening (4:30) rush hours.\n• Last-service warning: 45 minutes before the first of your lines stops for the day.\n\nAt most 3 a day, at least an hour apart, and none on Fridays.\n\nIt is planned on your phone from the lines' timetables, with no account needed, and nothing about you is sent to make it. The alerts arrive even when Guidy is closed.\n\nTo turn them off, use the switches under \"Notifications\": one for each kind, or the top one for all of them.",
